<title>ISRAEL: Bank of Israel buys back government bonds.</title>
<headline>Bank of Israel buys back government bonds.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Israel repurchased government bonds for the worth of 250 million shekels but received supply totalling 1.254 billion shekels.</p>
<p>The central bank said only 354 million shekels of the offers was at market price, at which price the bank was buying.</p>
</text>
